am> I think these are good, except for the no_doorway. I think that should
am> appear as the corridor symbol '#' rather than as the floor symbol '.'.

Consider this room:

	#...-----	####-----
	#.......|	##......|
	#.@.....-	##@.....-
	#|r.....|	#|r.....|
	#|......|	#|......|
	#+......|	#+......|
	 -----|--	 -----|--
	      #		      #
	(default)	(suggested)

With the default symbols, as a rule, you can see over and walk
diagonally from any '.' square.

Also, consider a dark room with completely munched walls:

	 ......		 ######
	 .    .##	 #    ###
	#.    .		##    #
	 ......		 ######

To use '#' in this fashion would be more confusing as to what areas
are visible.  However, if you prefer '#', you can set the no-door
symbol to it with the "graphics" option.  The '/' command would even
identify it correctly as "a corridor (or a doorway)  (a doorway)".

-3.


